                rdfs:label "the overallintent"@en ;
                rdfs:comment "meme-id: terrorism_is_one_of_the_only_areas_where_they_do_most_of_the_work_and_none_of_them_get_the_credit; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows a large pile of firearms in a metal cart, overlaid with text that reads: 'terrorism is one of the only areas where they do most of the work and none of them get the credit.' The visual of firearms is juxtaposed with the text to imply that 'they' (likely referring to law enforcement, military, or government agencies) are responsible for combating terrorism, but are not acknowledged or credited for their efforts. This meme is harmful because it promotes a false equivalence by suggesting that the work done to prevent or combat terrorism is somehow 'uncredited' or 'unappreciated,' while simultaneously using the image of weapons to imply violence or danger. The meme may be intended to provoke debate or outrage, but it risks normalizing or glorifying violence and could be used to justify or downplay the role of state actors in counter-terrorism operations. It does not target any specific protected group with hate or abuse, but its message is potentially dangerous as it could encourage a distorted view of the role of state actors in maintaining security, and may be used to justify or rationalize violence or militarization. The meme is not explicitly abusive, cyberbullying, misogynistic, or propagandistic in the sense of promoting a specific political agenda, but its harmful potential lies in its potential to normalize or glorify violence and to misrepresent the role of state actors in counter-terrorism."@en ;
                :extractionMethod "llm_extraction_huggingface" ;
                :extractedFrom "45976.png" ;
                :extractionTimestamp "2025-12-16T02:00:22.247493" .

